"program_narrative": "Program RTNCDE00 is a called subprogram (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING RC-REQUEST-AREA, laid out by copybook RTNCODE) that provides a standard return-code service to other programs. The caller sets RC-REQUEST-TYPE and the program dispatches to one of five operations: initialise the return-code area (I), record a new return code (S), return the current and highest codes (G), log the current code to DB2 table RTNCODES (L), or summarise logged codes for a program and time window (A). Recording a code keeps the highest code seen and classifies the new code as success (0), warning (1-4), error (5-8) or severe (any other value). The program reads and writes only the caller's linkage area and the DB2 table RTNCODES (one INSERT, one aggregate SELECT); there are no files and no loops. Error conditions handled: a failed INSERT or SELECT (SQLCODE not 0) sets RC-RESPONSE-CODE to 8; an unrecognised request type performs nothing.",
